{"name":"Bonfire Night","hex":"#de6a41","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bonfire Night","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Synonym of Guy Fawkes Night.","Synonym of Eleventh Night (“night before 12 July”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bonfire_Night"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonfire Night","blocks":[{"text":"Bonfire Night is a name given to various yearly events marked by bonfires and fireworks. These include Guy Fawkes Night in Great Britain; All Hallows' Eve ; May Eve ; Midsummer Eve/Saint John's Eve ; the Eleventh Night among Northern Ireland Protestants; and the Feast of the Assumption among Northern Ireland Catholics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Bonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg/330px-Bonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonfire_Night"},{"title":"Bonfire","blocks":[{"text":"A bonfire is a large and controlled outdoor fire, used for waste disposal or as part of a religious feast, such as Saint John's Eve."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg/330px-Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonfire"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg/500px-Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg/1280px-Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg/500px-Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fireworks display at a park in Worcestershire, United Kingdom","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Bonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg/500px-Bonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Bonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg/1280px-Bonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Bonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg/500px-Bonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"On the beaches of Duindorp (pictured) and Scheveningen, both part of The Hague, teams annually compete to build the world's largest bonfire[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABonfire_2018%2C_The_Hague%2C_preparations_on_31_December_2017.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Jahresfeuer_ganz1Ausschn.png/500px-Jahresfeuer_ganz1Ausschn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Jahresfeuer_ganz1Ausschn.png/500px-Jahresfeuer_ganz1Ausschn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Distribution of Funkenfeuer in Alemannic Europe, France and Northern Italy. Red shows traditions of Funkensonntag (the Sunday following Ash Wednesday), blue shows traditions of 1 March.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJahresfeuer_ganz1Ausschn.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Dan_Hadani_collection_%28990048345660205171%29.jpg/500px-Dan_Hadani_collection_%28990048345660205171%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Dan_Hadani_collection_%28990048345660205171%29.jpg/1280px-Dan_Hadani_collection_%28990048345660205171%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Dan_Hadani_collection_%28990048345660205171%29.jpg/500px-Dan_Hadani_collection_%28990048345660205171%